&lt;p&gt;Datadog is looking for a resourceful and creative&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Associate Field Marketing Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to lead event strategy and execution for Datadog&#39;s AI product line across the East and Canada region. This role is ideal for someone who is passionate about AI and developer communities, enjoys getting hands-on with technical audiences, and wants to build a market-leading brand presence for Datadog&#39;s AI offerings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the NAMER Field Marketing team, you will own the strategy, planning, and execution of a mix of practitioner-focused events, hands-on workshops, and surround activations at major AI conferences. This role is critical to scaling awareness and adoption of Datadog&#39;s AI products, and to building durable relationships with AI customers, prospects, and the broader developer community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy, planning, and end-to-end execution of AI practitioner events, hands-on workshops, and meetups across the East and Canada&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead surround and off-site activations at major AI conferences (e.g., NVIDIA GTC, Ray Summit, AI Engineer Summit, and similar industry events) to build brand visibility and drive engagement with target audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Marketing and AI/ML product teams to translate Datadog&#39;s AI observability and LLM monitoring capabilities into compelling, technically credible event content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and continuously improve hands-on workshop curriculum and live demos that showcase Datadog&#39;s AI products to practitioners and technical decision-makers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable, repeatable event playbooks and toolkits so programs can be run consistently across multiple markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendors, venues, budgets, staffing, and on-site logistics, ensuring every event reflects Datadog&#39;s brand and delivers a seamless attendee experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Sales and Field Marketing to align event strategy with territory and pipeline priorities across NAMER&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, measure, and report on pipeline influence, attendee engagement, and program ROI, using data to continuously refine the event mix&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultivate and grow relationships with AI developer communities, meetup organizers, and local user groups to expand Datadog&#39;s reach and reputation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on the AI/ML landscape and competitive events calendar to identify new opportunities for Datadog to show up and stand out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-2 years of experience in field marketing, event marketing, or program management, ideally with technical, developer, or AI/ML audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine enthusiasm for AI and machine learning, with the curiosity to go deep enough on the product to speak to it credibly at events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience planning and running practitioner-focused events or hands-on workshops, from concept through post-event follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple events, vendors, and budgets simultaneously in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, comfortable presenting to and engaging with technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, cross-functional operator who partners naturally with Sales, Product Marketing, and Product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process-oriented mindset with an interest in building scalable, repeatable programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with marketing or sales tools (e.g., SFDC, Marketo) is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 50% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
