&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;662&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Privacy and AI Guidelines:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;662&quot;&gt;Any information you submit to Datadog as part of your application will be processed in accordance with Datadog’s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/applicant-candidate-privacy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/applicant-candidate-privacy/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Applicant and Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. For information on our AI policy, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.datadoghq.com/legal/interviewing-at-datadog-ai-guidelines/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Interviewing at Datadog AI Guidelines&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Developers are shipping more code than ever, accelerated by AI-assisted development and increasingly complex software delivery workflows. As a Product Manager II on the Developer Engagement team, you&#39;ll help bring Datadog&#39;s insights and automation directly into the tools developers use every day, making software delivery faster, safer, and more efficient. You&#39;ll define customer-facing experiences that connect Datadog&#39;s observability, CI/CD, testing, security, and AI capabilities with pull requests, code reviews, and developer workflows. This role offers the opportunity to work closely with customers, engineering, design, and go-to-market teams while shaping the future of software delivery for developers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with customers, developers, platform engineering teams, and internal stakeholders to understand software delivery challenges and identify opportunities to improve developer workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product strategy and roadmap for developer-facing experiences within pull requests, code reviews, and source code management platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across Software Delivery products to surface actionable insights from CI/CD Optimization, Test Optimization, Code Coverage, Code Security, Deployment Gates, Bits AI, and future capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across source code ecosystems including GitHub, GitLab, Azure DevOps, Bitbucket, and enterprise environments to deliver scalable integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering teams to connect Datadog signals with recommendations, AI-assisted workflows, generated fixes, and future automated remediation experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure product success using customer adoption, engagement, feedback, and business outcomes while partnering with Sales, Product Marketing, Solutions Engineering, Customer Success, and Support to drive successful launches and customer adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 3–5 years of product management experience building developer products, technical platforms, or software engineering tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand modern software development workflows including code review, testing, CI/CD pipelines, deployment processes, APIs, webhooks, and source code management platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You demonstrate strong customer empathy and use customer research, product analytics, and business data to make informed product decisions and prioritize tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re curious about AI and excited to apply AI capabilities to improve developer productivity, software delivery, and release safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate effectively across engineering, design, and go-to-market teams while driving alignment and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with developer tools, CI/CD platforms, testing products, AI coding assistants, enterprise developer workflows, or previous software engineering experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Datadog values people from all walks of life. We know not everyone will meet all the above qualifications on day one. That’s okay. If you’re passionate about technology and want to grow your experience, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and Growth:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build products that improve software delivery for thousands of engineering teams around the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with experienced product managers, engineers, designers, and go-to-market teams across Datadog.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape the future of AI-powered developer experiences and software delivery workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own customer-facing initiatives with measurable product and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across the full software development lifecycle, from code creation through production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow your career in a collaborative, customer-focused organization that values continuous learning and innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benefits and Growth listed above may vary based on the country of your employment and the nature of your employment with Datadog.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits and Growth listed above may vary based on the country of your employment and the nature of your employment with Datadog.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
