&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced Senior Partner Manager to lead and scale Datadog&#39;s alliances with major Indian Global Systems Integrators (GSIs),&amp;nbsp; including - Wipro, Tech Mahindra, and Cognizant. This is a high-impact role responsible for driving partner-sourced pipeline, co-sell motions, and joint go-to-market initiatives in a global capacity. You will own the strategy and day-to-day execution of these strategic relationships, working closely with regional sales, marketing, and legal teams to unlock new revenue and expand Datadog&#39;s footprint through the Indian GSI ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute strategic plans to maximise customer success, partnership growth, and revenue opportunities across targeted Global Indian Systems Integrator partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive joint solution development, go-to-market initiatives, pipeline generation, and delivery excellence with partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with Datadog leaders and partner executives, securing alignment, influence, and commitment to shared priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Regional Partner Sales Managers responsible for GSI relationships, as well as cross-functional teams including Partner Solution Architecture, Marketing, Legal, and Deal Desk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and manage partnership agreements, order language, and contractual terms, including MSP addendums and pass-through obligations, in coordination with Legal and Deal Desk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate partner-sourced net-new pipeline and revenue, while identifying and recruiting additional practice areas or business units within existing GSI partners to expand the scope of the partnership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of partner-facing, quota-carrying business development experience, with a track record of building strategic relationships with Indian Global Systems Integrators at a cloud services or SaaS organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the Indian GSI landscape, with established relationships across organisations such as Wipro, Tech Mahindra, and Cognizant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to quickly understand technical concepts; including observability, security, cloud infrastructure, and AI/LLM monitoring, and translate them into clear, partner-relevant business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel 40% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
