&lt;p&gt;Datadog is looking for a Social Media Manager to advance our social media program. This role sits at the intersection of content creation, strategy, and corporate communications — owning the day-to-day execution of Datadog&#39;s social presence while helping shape how social supports our broader comms and marketing mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll report to our Senior Group Manager of Corporate Communications, while working in close partnership with the Senior Social Media Manager and the rest of the Corporate Communications team. This is a role for someone who is equal parts creative and analytical: you can write a scroll-stopping post and explain exactly why it worked.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Datadog, we place value in our office culture - the relationships and collaboration it builds and the creativity it brings to the table. We operate as a hybrid workplace to ensure our Datadogs can create a work-life harmony that best fits them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the content calendar and day-to-day execution across social channels, including Instagram, LinkedIn, and X.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute social communication plans for product announcements, launches, global events, and other key company initiatives in partnership with communications, marketing, and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and manage social content and programs that showcase Datadog, including employee advocacy initiatives, internal and external newsletters, and content supporting sponsored and Datadog-hosted events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor social channels and engage with relevant conversations, identifying cultural moments and routing mentions that require broader support to the appropriate internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze social performance and translate results into actionable insights and reporting for executives and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Senior Social Media Manager and larger Corporate Communications team to continually refine Datadog’s social strategy, processes, and approach to audience engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 4–6 years of experience in social media strategy and content creation, ideally within a corporate communications, marketing, or brand marketing function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a strong writer and editor with excellent attention to detail and the ability to develop engaging content for distinct audiences and channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand how social media works alongside media relations, executive communications, paid opportunities, and broader integrated communications programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience using social media analytics and management platforms, such as Sprout Social or Hootsuite, and translating performance data into insights for senior audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can manage multiple channels, projects, and stakeholders while collaborating effectively across a large organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re curious about social platforms, trends, culture, and emerging technologies, including opportunities to use tools such as large language models to improve social media workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
